---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ScenarioPlayer from '../components/ScenarioPlayer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Hop — the network that finds a way"
  description="Hop is a delay-tolerant mesh: end-to-end encrypted datagrams that hop device to device — over Bluetooth, LoRa, the internet — until they reach the person or service you meant. Held, never dropped. One transport every offline app builds on."
  path="/"
>
  <!-- hero: the scenario player is the pitch -->
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom:28px;">
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px;">Delay-tolerant mesh transport</div>
      <h1 style="max-width:none;margin:0 auto;">The network that finds a way.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin:20px auto 0;">
        Encrypted datagrams hop device to device — over Bluetooth, LoRa, the internet — until they
        reach the person or service you meant. No tower required. Held, never dropped.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta" style="justify-content:center;">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/quickstart/">Quickstart →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/docs/">Read the protocol</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-bottom:clamp(40px,6vw,72px);">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ScenarioPlayer />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- the narrow waist / build on Hop -->
  <section class="band band-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Why one protocol covers all of it</div>
        <h2>One layer. Every offline app.</h2>
        <p>Disaster, off-grid sensors, a region cut off, a phone with no plan — same problem: no
           reliable path, right now. Most offline products rebuild that transport and weld it to a
           single app. Hop is that layer, done once — a sealed, store-and-forward datagram. The
           narrow waist for intermittent networks: many bearers below, many apps above.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="layerstack">
        <div class="lrow">
          <span class="lvl">Apps</span>
          <div class="chips">
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/messaging/">Messaging</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/sync/">Data sync</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/files/">File transfer</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/web/">Offline web</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/telemetry/">Telemetry</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lrow">
          <span class="lvl">Semantics</span>
          <div class="chips">
            <a class="lchip code" href="/docs/hops/">hops://</a>
            <a class="lchip code" href="/docs/hps/">hps://</a>
            <a class="lchip code" href="/docs/streams/">streams</a>
            <a class="lchip code" href="/docs/hns/">HNS</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lrow waist">
          <span class="lvl">Waist</span>
          <div class="chips">
            <a class="lchip code" href="/docs/hdp/">hdp://</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/hdp/">end-to-end encrypted, store-and-forward datagrams</a>
          </div>
          <span class="waisttag">the waist</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lrow bearer">
          <span class="lvl">Bearer</span>
          <div class="chips">
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/ble/">Bluetooth LE</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/l2cap/">L2CAP</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/tcp/">TCP / WebSocket</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/bearers/">LoRa, Wi-Fi Aware…</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- how it's monetized -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">The model</div>
        <h2>The library is free. The cloud is the product.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The device does the work, so the SDK is open and free. The cloud backbone
           costs money to run — so that's what you pay for, only when you use it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="layers">
        <div class="layer">
          <div class="lv">Layer 0</div>
          <h3>Open SDK</h3>
          <p>Embed <code>hop-core</code> on iOS &amp; Android. Source-available, free forever.</p>
          <div class="who">Free</div>
        </div>
        <div class="layer paid">
          <div class="lv">Layer 1</div>
          <h3>Hosted backbone</h3>
          <p>Managed relay fleet, durable mailboxes, internet egress, <code>hops://</code> endpoints.</p>
          <div class="who">Usage-based</div>
        </div>
        <div class="layer">
          <div class="lv">Layer 2</div>
          <h3>Commercial license</h3>
          <p>Terms beyond the FSL non-compete, for products that need them.</p>
          <div class="who">Enterprise</div>
        </div>
        <div class="layer">
          <div class="lv">Layer 3</div>
          <h3>Private &amp; mission</h3>
          <p>On-prem fleets, private backbones, and support for field operations.</p>
          <div class="who">Solutions</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- audience doors -->
  <section class="band band-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="doors">
        <a class="door" href="/developers/">
          <div class="kicker">For developers</div>
          <h3>Put your app on the mesh.</h3>
          <p>A pure-Rust core with iOS &amp; Android bindings, HTTP-over-mesh (<code>hops://</code>),
             pub/sub, and DNSSEC-backed naming. Embed it and your app keeps working when the
             network doesn't.</p>
          <div class="go">Explore the SDK →</div>
        </a>
        <a class="door" href="/business/">
          <div class="kicker">For business</div>
          <h3>Connectivity that doesn't depend on connectivity.</h3>
          <p>Events, field operations, maritime, rural, response, public safety &amp; defense. Run on
             the managed backbone, or stand up a private fleet of your own — licensing and support
             included.</p>
          <div class="go">See solutions →</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- cta -->
  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Build for where the network goes dark.</h2>
      <p>Embed the free SDK today. Add the cloud backbone when you need to reach across the world.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/quickstart/">Quickstart →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
